refactor(voice): remove local Whisper (whisper.cpp) — API + browser paths only

Drops the bundled local transcription engine entirely; voice input now
resolves: OpenAI whisper-1 (when an OpenAI key is set) → browser Speech
API fallback.

Removed:
- Rust: modules/whisper.rs (584 lines — model catalog, download manager,
  transcribe worker, abort plumbing), whisper-rs dependency (whisper.cpp
  bindings), the 7 whisper_* command registrations, WhisperManager state,
  and the .part.<pid> download-temp GC block in lib.rs.
- Frontend: whisper native bindings + types in native.ts, the local
  transcription path in useWhisperRecording (decode-to-16k-f32 pipeline,
  base64 bridge, duration-scaled timeouts), the "Local voice
  transcription" settings block (model list, download/remove/select,
  progress bar) from General → Settings, and the whisperModelId
  preference with its accessors.

Kept: cloud transcribeBlob (whisper-1 via the OpenAI key), the browser
SpeechRecognition fallback (no key needed), mic watchdogs and
permission-denied handling — unchanged behavior for both remaining
routes.

Rationale: local CPU whisper was slow (minutes/clip on the larger
models), shipped a heavy native dep, and the cloud path is the primary
UX anyway.

cargo check clean (clippy warning in mcp.rs pre-existing), tsc clean,
286 tests pass.
